<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-FREE STATE-BORDER MATCH ENDS IN DRAW.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-FREE STATE-BORDER MATCH ENDS IN DRAW.</headline>
<dateline>BLOEMFONTEIN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Border's chances of glory in</p>
<p>the Supersport series were effectively dashed when they drew</p>
<p>their match against Free State at Springbok Park on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Border failed to rise to the challenge after Free State set</p>
<p>them a target of 324 in 82 overs having declared their innings</p>
<p>closed on 297 for nine -- not an impossible target on this</p>
<p>traditionally batsman friendly wicket.</p>
<p>Border did make an effort in the middle session when they</p>
<p>put on 119 runs with skipper Piet Strydom hitting six fours and</p>
<p>one six in his 31.</p>
<p>However, after Strydom was bowled by right-arm spinner Kosie</p>
<p>Venter, Steven Pope and Ian Howell closed up shop and the game</p>
<p>yawned its way to a draw.</p>
